
## Operator workflow

1. Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/compiler/common/error_types_spec.spl`.
2. Every scenario must pass; a failure is a regression in the
   behavior under test.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers the interpreter and native lanes for the constructs
asserted here; platform-specific behavior is out of scope.
"""

        it("reports argument count mismatches with both counts", fn() -> ():
            # @req REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
            step("build a count-mismatch error")
            # oracle: expected 2 vs found 3 are the counts passed in
            val msg = argument_count_mismatch(2, 3).message
            expect(msg.find("2") ?? -1).to_be_greater_than(-1)
            expect(msg.find("3") ?? -1).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        )
    )
